<http://shaclshapes.org/noteBasinShapeProperty> rdf:type <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#PropertyShape> ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: Feature description: An undersea basin in Bounty Haven at the southern end of Hawea / Bligh Sound. History/Origin/Meaning: Named in association with Bounty Haven, which Stokes named in assocation with Hawea / Bligh Sound under the mistaken impression that feature was named for Bligh of the Bounty."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: Shown as Venezuelan Basin in the ACUF Gazetteer."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: This feature has an elongated shape. Minimum depth (m): 5000. Maximum depth (m): 5860. Total relief (m): 860. Dimension: 50 km x 13 km."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "GEBCO: associated meeting, proposer and year of proposal: Associated meeting: SCUFN-15. Proposer: Chilean Hydrographic Office (SHOA). History: 2002."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> """GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: Discoverer: Indonesian Navy Survey Ship "KRI Rigel 933". Year of discovery: 2021. History: Named in association with the nearby Aurora Bank."""@en ;
