<http://shaclshapes.org/noteCanyonsShapeProperty> rdf:type <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#PropertyShape> ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: Taken from Allen J. R. L., Nigerian Continental Margin: bottom sediments, submarine morphology and geological evolution (1964)."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Additional information: This feature comprises three canyons on the upper continental slope, located approximately 115 km W-NW of Cape Egmont on the W coast of the North Island of New Zealand. They extend westwards towards the southern end of New Caledonia Trough. The name first appeared on Oceanic Bathymetry Series (OBS) chart 'Cook' in 1991. Minimum depth (m): 200. Maximum depth (m): 1000. Total relief (m): 800. Dimension/size: 25 km x 15 km."@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "Coordinates in ACUF: Latitude: 13.616667; Longitude: -80.166667"@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> """GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: Discoverer: British vessel HMS "Endurance". Year of discovery: 1985. History: Named from its geographic location, on the shelf break in front of São Tomé Cape, a peninsula in the north of Rio de Janeiro State, Brazil. This feature was formed by accumulation of sediments from the Paraíba do Sul River."""@en ;
  <http://example.org/example> "GEBCO: discoverer and year of discovery: History: Named after Reginald (Reg) C. Sprigg (1919-1994), geologist with the South Australian Geological Survey."@en ;
  <http://shaclshapes.org/confidence> 7.725E-1 ;
  <http://shaclshapes.org/support> "309"^^xsd:int ;
